{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380364-does-a-fledgling-has-to-be-a-thin-blood","id":1380364,"title":"Does a Fledgling has to be a Thin-blood?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-11T05:32:53-07:00","id":1380364,"title":"Does a Fledgling has to be a Thin-blood?","content":"So I am a new Storyteller who is going to run his first Vampire: The Masquerade session around May. And I have been trying to wrap my head around this. Most of my players want to play as Fledgelings to feel the struggle of becoming a new vampire. But they also want to have a clan as well. In V5, is it a must for a fledgling to be thin-blooded? Or can a fledgling have a clan and access to its powers?<br /> <br /> I'm sorry if the question is weird. I'm still not sure about the difference between a fledgling and a thin-blod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24239-the-keeper","name":"The Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:52:48-07:00","id":1380375,"title":"","content":"No, a fledgling doesn't have to be a thin-blood. Fledglings are any newly embraced vampires that are still under the protection of their sires and can be any generation. Thin-bloods are vampires with such weakened blood that they don't manifest clan traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:56:13-07:00","id":1380376,"title":"","content":"Fledglings are really just brand new vampires (of any generation) that haven't been released by their sire yet. For the purposes of V5 character generation, brand new vampires use the Childer guidelines on p. 137 and can either be Thin-Bloods or 12th/13th Generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:11:03-07:00","id":1380410,"title":"","content":"Thinblood is for any vampire embraced post generation 13. So if your players are 13th or lower they are normal vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:53:20-07:00","id":1380468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380364-does-a-fledgling-has-to-be-a-thin-blood?p=1380410#post1380410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinblood is for any vampire embraced post generation 13. So if your players are 13th or lower they are normal vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>that is not entirely true since V20. To be Thin-blooded is a special property of the blood. Theoretically, Vampires of every generation can produce Thin-Bloods, it is just not very probable above the 13th (cant remember the page but it is described in BJD). But since this question is about V5 and generations doesn\u2019t reale matter for Thin Bloods, that is just a footnote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:03:12-07:00","id":1380472,"title":"","content":"No, you really don\u2019t have to be a Thin-Blood, it is even rather the exaction. Maybe you think that, because of Bloodlines 2, where Thin Blood is the default state and even later the character is \u201eupgraded\u201c to a clan. But that is extremely rare in the P&amp;P version.<br /> <br /> A fledgling can even be quite powerful, if he is sired from a low generation Vampire, he just don\u2019t know how to use his power jet.<br /> <br /> Usually, a vampire is of the same Clan as his sire, just one generation higher. There is a chance that a newly sired vampire ends up as a Caitiff, a Vampire with out Clan. What that happens is often not entirely clear. The same with Thin Bloods. Theoretically every Vampire can accidentally produce a Thin blood, but it is extremely improbable if the Sire in question is of generation 12 or higher. Vampires of Generation 13, 14, 15 and higher have a high chance of producing Thin bloods, if their children survive at all (dying is still the most probable outcome if a human is unlucky enough to be sired by a 13+ generation Vampire, that is why thin bloods are still a relatively small part of Vampire society and not all over the place).<br /> <br /> But you can find all about that in the chapter about character creation and generation in the V5 Core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","user":"Sethos","date":". 04-11-2020, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T01:25:29-07:00","id":1380598,"title":"","content":"In V20 that might be true, but in V5 all 14+ are thin bloods.<br /> <br /> But the Childer character generation option gives you the option to be either &quot;14-16 and thinblood&quot; or &quot;12 or 13 and having a clan&quot;.<br /> <br /> Fledgling is just a really young Childer as others have pointed out, so would still fall into that category as well. And technically once you're released you become a Neonate. &quot;Childer&quot; is something you'll always be. You will always be the Childe of your Sire, even if you're both 2000 years old, it doesn't denote age at all. So I'm a bit unhappy with the names for the categories here.<br /> <br /> And heck if your ST is fine with it, you can just as well be a 10th generation fledgling or young childe (Why would the 9th generation not embrace anymore if they need a new servant/cannon fodder). It's just not immediately supported by the rules in the character creation chapter, but its very easy to change, and everything else doesn't contradict it either. Min. Blood Potency for a 10th gen is still 1, so I would give them that, and then just continue like the &quot;Childer&quot; Sections says.<br /> Same goes for having a 13th generation Ancillae. Even in the 1700s 12th gen were around and did embrace. Max BP for a 13th gen is 3, so the starting BP of 2 works fine there as well, and so just use that section.<br /> <br /> It's just that the book gives you a baseline to keep powerlevels across the coterie even I suppose, but as a ST you can mess with it, no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T01:33:49-07:00","id":1380599,"title":"","content":"A fledgling is any new vampire. If the Antes are up and about there could be 4th Gen fledglings about the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T05:53:44-07:00","id":1380922,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry that I'm still confused. I'm currently planning on running two chronicles and one of them is for newer generations vampires. I mentioned to the players that their vampire age should be at least 1 night and maximum would be 15 years. I assumed that it counts as fledgling. But I'd like to follow the lore as it is, even 'tho I haven't understood it fully.<br /> <br /> So within that rage of 1 night - 15 years, that means they're all thin-bloods? Or they can have clans?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm sorry that I'm still confused.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24239-the-keeper","name":"The Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T09:34:36-07:00","id":1380993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380364-does-a-fledgling-has-to-be-a-thin-blood?p=1380922#post1380922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry that I'm still confused. I'm currently planning on running two chronicles and one of them is for newer generations vampires. I mentioned to the players that their vampire age should be at least 1 night and maximum would be 15 years. I assumed that it counts as fledgling. But I'd like to follow the lore as it is, even 'tho I haven't understood it fully.<br /> <br /> So within that rage of 1 night - 15 years, that means they're all thin-bloods? Or they can have clans?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm sorry that I'm still confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can have clans. <br /> <br /> Thinbloods are only if you have been embraced by a 13th generation vampire or higher. If a character is embraced by a 12th generation or lower, they will never be a thinblood. It's just that characters older than 15 years are not allowed for thinbloods normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:25:19-07:00","id":1381011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380364-does-a-fledgling-has-to-be-a-thin-blood?p=1380922#post1380922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry that I'm still confused. I'm currently planning on running two chronicles and one of them is for newer generations vampires. I mentioned to the players that their vampire age should be at least 1 night and maximum would be 15 years. I assumed that it counts as fledgling. But I'd like to follow the lore as it is, even 'tho I haven't understood it fully.<br /> <br /> So within that rage of 1 night - 15 years, that means they're all thin-bloods? Or they can have clans?<br /> <br /> Again, I'm sorry that I'm still confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fledgling is just a status in regards to age post-Embrace. Much like neonates, ancillae, Elder, or Methuselah. Fledgling is newly embraced, but not around long enough to be away from their sire.<br /> <br /> Thin-blood is a status of the vitae itself. Thin-bloods have such weak vitae that they do not show traditional clan attributes, possibly some vampire attributes (can walk in sunlight, eat food, procreate). They are essentially undead ghouls. They can become stronger through diablerie, but they are between ghoul and day 1 13th generation vampire when it comes to initial power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T19:02:16-07:00","id":1381501,"title":"","content":"Alright, thank you so much for the explanations! Really clears up my confusion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24239-the-keeper","name":"The Keeper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T07:16:09-07:00","id":1381916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Keeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380364-does-a-fledgling-has-to-be-a-thin-blood?p=1380922#post1380922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So within that rage of 1 night - 15 years, that means they're all thin-bloods? Or they can have clans?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I know where the confusion might be coming from.<br /> <br /> Thin-blood has nothing to do with age. Thin bloods have been around forever. In the Dark Ages books they were a possiblity. In V20 and previous editions they were possible.<br /> But till recently thin-bloods had been actively hunted down and killed whenever they were found. Many cities had the position of a &quot;Scourge&quot; who's primary job it often was to find and kill them. A lot of old vampires saw them as Harbingers Of The End Times and just murdered them whenever they found them.<br /> <br /> It was only recently that they were allowed to survive, probably because they're just too many of them, or that the Camarilla has other problems (like the Second Inquistion) or that they actually found a few sympathetic princes or elders who gave them their protection, etc. Likely to use them in their schemes, but that doesn't matter for this.<br /> <br /> Point is, there's just not many thin bloods around anymore that are older than 15 or 20 years. Hence why they only appear in the first age-bracket. But they have nothing to do directly with age.<br /> <br /> =====<br /> <br /> Now on the topic of fledgling again. Fledgling is just a term used, and it certainly refers to age, but also is sort of a rank. A fledgling can not fly on its own yet, and is still under the wing of its sire. That's where the name comes from, I suppose.<br /> <br /> During that time they're taught the rules and laws and traditions and what not. Or at least thats the idea. As a fledgling the Sire is FULLY responsible for their childe. The childe kills a human, it's the Sire who's on the hook. The fledgling attacks a priced ghoul of the prince in Ellysium, it's probably the Sire's head that's rolling (and the fledgling's too).<br /> <br /> How long is someone a fledgling? Well theoretically till the sire thinks they're ready and presents them to the Prince and the city at Ellysium and releases them. The Prince can deny that and say they still need to learn etc. But how long that is, fully depends on the clan. If a Gangrel embraces someone in the wilderness its possible he goes &quot;Well you're a vampire now. You need to drink blood. Oh and sun and fire bad. Bye now, I'll maybe find you in a decade again to see if you survived&quot; (in a city with a Prince that wouldn't fly just like that). While the Ventrue are notorious for keeping their fledglings for years or even decades before they think they're ready to be unleashed on the world. Most other clans fall somewhere in the middle there.<br /> <br /> In general its rather boring playing a fledgling, especially since they're so tied to their sire that they're often not allowed to do their own things yet. In my opinion its best to start somewhere after the release, and they're fresh neonates.<br /> <br /> Not to confuse with the Neonate in that section. Neonate in the LORE is just a vampire that is not a fledgeling anymore but is not an Ancilla yet. Generally between a year or whenever they were released and about 100 years old.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T13:20:04-07:00","id":1381969,"title":"","content":"I like to help al the time, but I kind of wonder if OP has read the core book. Everything is explained there pretty clear, if he just searches for the words Fledgling and Thin-Blood. I honestly don\u2019t understand how that can be still unclear after reading the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T16:11:23-07:00","id":1382004,"title":"","content":"There was a time when the antedeluvians were fledgelings. Other than having ridonkulas blood-pools, they had plain old fledgling stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}